description:
README.md:34-44 shows:

  struct MyBackend { /* db pool, etc. */ }
  impl MetadataBackend for MyBackend { /* ... */ }

This compiles only if MyBackend also impls JmapBackend (the supertrait). The example is not runnable as written and a contributor following 'How to use' will hit a compile error and need to dig elsewhere.

Audience: a new contributor reading the README to figure out how to integrate. The README's job is to be a step-by-step that works. The current state is 'do all the steps and also do this implicit other step we don't mention'.

What would make it clear: either (a) show the JmapBackend impl too (long), or (b) reference the trait docs explicitly: '// You also need to impl JmapBackend (the supertrait). See [link to jmap-server::JmapBackend].'
